import VOA.Examples.TripletLattice
import VOA.Examples.TripletScreening
import VOA.Examples.TripletW2
import VOA.Core.VOASubalgebraGenerated

/-!
# The triplet vertex algebra `W(p)` as a subalgebra of the deformed lattice VOA

Three earlier files supply the pieces:

* `Examples.TripletLattice` — the **ambient**: `tripletLatticeVOA p hp`, the rank-one lattice VOA
  of `L_p = ℤα`, `⟨α,α⟩ = 2p`, deformed by the Feigin–Fuchs background charge
  `λ_p = ((p−1)/(2p))·α`.  Its central charge is `c_p = 1 − 6(p−1)²/p` and its grading is the
  deformed one, `wt(e^{mα}) = q_p(m) = p m² − (p−1)m`.
* `Examples.TripletScreening` — the **generators**: `Q = (e^α)₍₀₎` (the long screening operator),
  `F = e^{−α}`, `H = Q F`, `E = Q H`, all of deformed weight `2p − 1`, with `Q³F = 0` and `H ≠ 0`.
* `Core.VOASubalgebraGenerated` — the **closure operation**: `VOASubalgebra.generated W S`, the
  smallest vertex operator subalgebra of `W` containing a set `S`, and `generatedVOA W S`, the
  `VertexOperatorAlgebra` structure it carries (via the imported `VOASubalgebra.toVOA`).

This file assembles them.

## Main definitions

* `omegaTrip p`, `Etrip p`, `Htrip p`, `Ftrip p` — the four generating states of `V_{L_p}`
  (the deformed conformal vector and the three screening states at `α = α_p`).
* `tripGens p : Set (LatModuleGen (latP p))` — the generating set `{ω_λ, E, H, F}`.
* `tripletW p hp : VOASubalgebra (tripletLatticeVOA p hp)` — **the triplet algebra `W(p)`**,
  defined as `VOASubalgebra.generated _ (tripGens p)`.
* `tripletWVOA p hp : VertexOperatorAlgebra (tripletW p hp).carrier` — the induced VOA
  structure on its carrier.

## Main results

* `tripletW_centralCharge : (tripletWVOA p hp).centralCharge = 1 − 6(p−1)²/p`.
* **Weight-homogeneity of the generators.**  `omegaTrip_mem_grading` (weight `2`),
  `Etrip_mem_grading`, `Htrip_mem_grading`, `Ftrip_mem_grading` (all weight `2p − 1`), and the
  operator forms `L0_omegaTrip`, `L0_Etrip`, `L0_Htrip`, `L0_Ftrip`.  Consequently
  `piHom_omegaTrip_self` … `piHom_Ftrip_zero` and `tripGens_homogeneous`: every homogeneous
  projection either fixes a generator or kills it, so it never leaves the generating set — the
  point flagged by the `mem_generated` induction principle, whose `piHom` clause is unavoidable
  because gradedness is an axiom of `VOASubalgebra`.
* **Non-degeneracy** (the algebra is not vacuously trivial): `vacuum_mem_tripletW`,
  `omegaTrip_mem_tripletW`, `Etrip_mem_tripletW`, `Htrip_mem_tripletW`, `Ftrip_mem_tripletW`;
  `omegaTrip_ne_zero`, `Htrip_ne_zero`, `Ftrip_ne_zero`; `tripletW_carrier_ne_bot`; and
  `span_tripGens_le_tripletW`.
* **`p = 2` consistency check**: `tripletW_centralCharge_two` and
  `tripletW_centralCharge_eq_tripletW2` record that `W(2)` built here and the symplectic-fermion
  `SympFerm.tripletW2` have the *same central charge* `−2`.

## What is **not** proved

1. **`E ≠ 0` for general `p`.**  `Examples.TripletScreening` proves `H ≠ 0` (and `F ≠ 0` is
   immediate); `E = Q²F ≠ 0` is not proved in the library for general `p`.  At `p = 2` it holds
   (a few lines from library lemmas: certificate `L18Checks.Etrip_two_ne_zero`,
   `Notes/Textbook/certificates/L18_Checks.lean`; not a library theorem).  (For `p = 1` it is not even
   expected to be interesting: `L_1 = √2ℤ` is the `A₁` lattice and `2p − 1 = 1`.)
2. **`W(p) ≠ V_{L_p}`** for general `p`, i.e. that the subalgebra is proper.  At `p = 2` it holds
   (certificate `L18Checks.tripletW_two_carrier_ne_top`, same file; not a library theorem).  The
   identification of `tripletW p hp` with the kernel of the *short* screening (the literature's
   definition of `W(p)`) is not proved anywhere in the library.
3. **`W(2) ≅ SympFerm.tripletW2`.**  A VOA *isomorphism* is a research problem and is explicitly
   **not** claimed.  All that is recorded is the numerical agreement of central charges,
   `−2 = −2`; this is a consistency check, not an identification.
4. The **`W`-algebra structure** itself — that `span{E,H,F}` closes under the vertex products into
   a `𝔰𝔩₂`-triplet, or that `W(p)` is the kernel of `Q` — is untouched (see the "What is *not*
   here" section of `Examples.TripletScreening`).

## References
* Kausch, *Extended conformal algebras generated by a multiplet of primary fields*.
* Feigin–Gainutdinov–Semikhatov–Tipunin, *Logarithmic extensions of minimal models*.
* Adamović–Milas, *On the triplet vertex algebra `W(p)`*.
-/

set_option linter.style.longLine false

namespace VOA.LatGen.Wp

open scoped BigOperators TensorProduct
open Module (End)
open VOA VOA.IntegralLattice HeisenbergN
open VOA.LatGen VOA.LatGen.Triplet

/-! ## §1  The four generating states -/

/-- The deformed conformal vector `ω_{λ_p} = ω_{L_p} + λ_p(−2)|0⟩ ∈ V_{L_p}`; it is the conformal
vector of `tripletLatticeVOA p hp`. -/
noncomputable def omegaTrip (p : ℕ) : LatModuleGen (latP p) :=
  BgA.omegaBg (latP p) (lamP p)

/-- `F = e^{−α}`, the lowest triplet generator (deformed weight `2p − 1`). -/
noncomputable def Ftrip (p : ℕ) : LatModuleGen (latP p) :=
  Screen.Fscr (latP p) (alphaP p)

/-- `H = Q F = ε(α,−α)·S_{2p−1}(α) ⊗ e⁰`, the middle triplet generator. -/
noncomputable def Htrip (p : ℕ) : LatModuleGen (latP p) :=
  Screen.Hscr (latP p) (alphaP p)

/-- `E = Q H = Q² F`, the top triplet generator. -/
noncomputable def Etrip (p : ℕ) : LatModuleGen (latP p) :=
  Screen.Escr (latP p) (alphaP p)

theorem omegaTrip_eq_conformalVector (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).conformalVector = omegaTrip p := rfl

/-- `α = 1 ∈ L_p` is non-zero. -/
theorem alphaP_ne_zero (p : ℕ) : alphaP p ≠ (0 : (latP p).carrier) := by
  intro h
  exact one_ne_zero (show (1 : ℤ) = 0 from h)

/-! ## §2  The generators are weight-homogeneous

`ω_λ` sits in deformed weight `2`; `E`, `H`, `F` all sit in deformed weight `2p − 1`.  For `F` this
is `Triplet.latChargeGen_neg_alpha_mem_grade`; for `H` and `E` we read the boson degree off
`Screen.Hscr_eq` / `Screen.Escr_eq` and feed it to `Triplet.mem_gradTrip_of_bigradα`. -/

/-- `ω_λ ∈ 𝒱₂`. -/
theorem omegaTrip_mem_grading (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    omegaTrip p ∈ (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).grading 2 :=
  (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).conformal_mem

/-- `F = e^{−α} ∈ 𝒱_{2p−1}`. -/
theorem Ftrip_mem_grading (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    Ftrip p ∈ (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).grading (2 * (p : ℤ) - 1) :=
  latChargeGen_neg_alpha_mem_grade p hp

/-- The Schur state `S_{2p−1}(α)` has boson degree `2p − 1`. -/
theorem vSchur_mem_gradingZN_alphaP (p : ℕ) :
    vSchur (latP p) (alphaP p) (2 * p - 1)
      ∈ gradingZN (rank (latP p)) (((2 * p - 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) :=
  mem_gradingZN_of_gradingWN (Screen.vSchur_mem_gradingWN (latP p) (alphaP p) (2 * p - 1))

/-- `H ∈ 𝒱_{2p−1}`: `H` is `S_{2p−1}(α)` (boson degree `2p−1`) in the charge-`0` sector, where the
deformed weight `q_p(0) = 0` adds nothing. -/
theorem Htrip_mem_grading (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    Htrip p ∈ (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).grading (2 * (p : ℤ) - 1) := by
  have hbi : latStateGen (latP p) (vSchur (latP p) (alphaP p) (2 * p - 1)) (0 : ℤ)
      ∈ bigradα (latP p) ((((2 * p - 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)), (0 : ℤ)) :=
    ⟨_, vSchur_mem_gradingZN_alphaP p, rfl⟩
  have hk : ((2 * p - 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + qZP p (0 : ℤ) = 2 * (p : ℤ) - 1 := by
    rw [qZP_zero]
    omega
  have hmem : latStateGen (latP p) (vSchur (latP p) (alphaP p) (2 * p - 1)) (0 : ℤ)
      ∈ gradTrip p (2 * (p : ℤ) - 1) :=
    mem_gradTrip_of_bigradα p (2 * (p : ℤ) - 1) (((2 * p - 1 : ℕ) : ℤ)) (0 : ℤ) hk hbi
  rw [Htrip, Screen.Hscr_eq (latP p) (alphaP p) p hp (latP_form_alpha p)]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hmem

/-- `E ∈ 𝒱_{2p−1}`: `E` is `EE(α)₍₋₁₎S_{2p−1}(α)` (boson degree `2p−2`) in the charge-`α` sector,
where the deformed weight `q_p(α) = 1` makes up the difference. -/
theorem Etrip_mem_grading (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    Etrip p ∈ (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).grading (2 * (p : ℤ) - 1) := by
  have hE : EEVec (latP p) (alphaP p) (-1) (vSchur (latP p) (alphaP p) (2 * p - 1))
      ∈ gradingZN (rank (latP p)) (((2 * p - 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + (-1)) :=
    Screen.EEVec_mem_gradingZN (latP p) (alphaP p) (-1) (vSchur_mem_gradingZN_alphaP p)
  have hbi : latStateGen (latP p)
      (EEVec (latP p) (alphaP p) (-1) (vSchur (latP p) (alphaP p) (2 * p - 1))) (alphaP p)
      ∈ bigradα (latP p) ((((2 * p - 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + (-1)), alphaP p) :=
    ⟨_, hE, rfl⟩
  have hk : (((2 * p - 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) + (-1)) + qZP p (alphaP p) = 2 * (p : ℤ) - 1 := by
    rw [alphaP, qZP_one]
    omega
  rw [Etrip, Screen.Escr_eq (latP p) (alphaP p) p hp (latP_form_alpha p)]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (mem_gradTrip_of_bigradα p _ _ _ hk hbi)

/-! ### Operator form of the weights -/

/-- `L₀^λ ω_λ = 2 ω_λ`. -/
theorem L0_omegaTrip (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).L 0 (omegaTrip p) = (2 : ℂ) • omegaTrip p := by
  have h := (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).L_zero_grading (omegaTrip p) (omegaTrip_mem_grading p hp)
  rw [h]
  norm_num

/-- `L₀^λ F = (2p−1) F`. -/
theorem L0_Ftrip (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).L 0 (Ftrip p) = (2 * (p : ℂ) - 1) • Ftrip p := by
  have h := (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).L_zero_grading (Ftrip p) (Ftrip_mem_grading p hp)
  rw [h]
  congr 1
  push_cast
  ring

/-- `L₀^λ H = (2p−1) H`. -/
theorem L0_Htrip (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).L 0 (Htrip p) = (2 * (p : ℂ) - 1) • Htrip p := by
  have h := (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).L_zero_grading (Htrip p) (Htrip_mem_grading p hp)
  rw [h]
  congr 1
  push_cast
  ring

/-- `L₀^λ E = (2p−1) E`. -/
theorem L0_Etrip (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).L 0 (Etrip p) = (2 * (p : ℂ) - 1) • Etrip p := by
  have h := (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).L_zero_grading (Etrip p) (Etrip_mem_grading p hp)
  rw [h]
  congr 1
  push_cast
  ring

/-! ## §3  The generating set and the subalgebra it generates -/

/-- **The generating set of `W(p)`**: the deformed conformal vector together with the three
screening states `E`, `H`, `F` of deformed weight `2p − 1`. -/
noncomputable def tripGens (p : ℕ) : Set (LatModuleGen (latP p)) :=
  {omegaTrip p, Etrip p, Htrip p, Ftrip p}

theorem omegaTrip_mem_tripGens (p : ℕ) : omegaTrip p ∈ tripGens p :=
  Set.mem_insert _ _

theorem Etrip_mem_tripGens (p : ℕ) : Etrip p ∈ tripGens p :=
  Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ (Set.mem_insert _ _)

theorem Htrip_mem_tripGens (p : ℕ) : Htrip p ∈ tripGens p :=
  Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ (Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ (Set.mem_insert _ _))

theorem Ftrip_mem_tripGens (p : ℕ) : Ftrip p ∈ tripGens p :=
  Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ (Set.mem_insert_of_mem _
    (Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ (Set.mem_singleton _)))

/-- **The triplet vertex algebra `W(p)`**: the vertex operator subalgebra of the deformed
lattice VOA `V_{L_p}` generated by the conformal vector and the three weight-`(2p−1)` screening
states `E = Q²e^{−α}`, `H = Qe^{−α}`, `F = e^{−α}`.

Being defined as a `VOASubalgebra.generated`, it is by construction the *smallest* subspace of
`V_{L_p}` that contains `𝟙`, `ω_λ`, `E`, `H`, `F`, is closed under every vertex product `u₍ₙ₎v`,
and is stable under the homogeneous projections. -/
noncomputable def tripletW (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) : VOASubalgebra (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) :=
  VOASubalgebra.generated (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) (tripGens p)

theorem tripletW_def (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    tripletW p hp = VOASubalgebra.generated (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) (tripGens p) := rfl

/-! ## §4  The induced vertex operator algebra structure and its central charge -/

/-- **`W(p)` is a vertex operator algebra**, namely the restriction of `V_{L_p}` to the
generated subalgebra (`VOASubalgebra.toVOA`, packaged as `VOASubalgebra.generatedVOA`). -/
noncomputable def tripletWVOA (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    VertexOperatorAlgebra (tripletW p hp).carrier :=
  VOASubalgebra.generatedVOA (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) (tripGens p)

/-- **The central charge of `W(p)` is `c_p = 1 − 6(p−1)²/p`** — the Feigin–Fuchs value.  A
subalgebra keeps the ambient conformal vector, hence the ambient central charge. -/
@[simp] theorem tripletW_centralCharge (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    (tripletWVOA p hp).centralCharge = 1 - 6 * ((p : ℂ) - 1) ^ 2 / (p : ℂ) := rfl

/-- The vertex operators of `W(p)` are the ambient ones. -/
@[simp] theorem tripletWVOA_Y_coe (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) (u : (tripletW p hp).carrier) (k : ℤ)
    (x : (tripletW p hp).carrier) :
    (((tripletWVOA p hp).Y u k x : (tripletW p hp).carrier) : LatModuleGen (latP p))
      = (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).Y u k x := rfl

/-- The vacuum of `W(p)` is the lattice vacuum `|0⟩`. -/
@[simp] theorem tripletWVOA_vacuum_coe (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    (((tripletWVOA p hp).vacuum : (tripletW p hp).carrier) : LatModuleGen (latP p))
      = latVacuumGen (latP p) := rfl

/-- The conformal vector of `W(p)` is the deformed one, `ω_{λ_p}`. -/
@[simp] theorem tripletWVOA_conformalVector_coe (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    (((tripletWVOA p hp).conformalVector : (tripletW p hp).carrier) : LatModuleGen (latP p))
      = omegaTrip p := rfl

/-! ## §5  Non-degeneracy

`W(p)` is not vacuously trivial: the vacuum, the conformal vector and the three generators all lie
in it, and `ω_λ`, `H`, `F` are non-zero states. -/

theorem vacuum_mem_tripletW (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    latVacuumGen (latP p) ∈ (tripletW p hp).carrier :=
  (tripletW p hp).vacuum_mem

theorem omegaTrip_mem_tripletW (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    omegaTrip p ∈ (tripletW p hp).carrier :=
  (tripletW p hp).conformal_mem

theorem Etrip_mem_tripletW (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    Etrip p ∈ (tripletW p hp).carrier :=
  VOASubalgebra.mem_generated_of_mem (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) (Etrip_mem_tripGens p)

theorem Htrip_mem_tripletW (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    Htrip p ∈ (tripletW p hp).carrier :=
  VOASubalgebra.mem_generated_of_mem (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) (Htrip_mem_tripGens p)

theorem Ftrip_mem_tripletW (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    Ftrip p ∈ (tripletW p hp).carrier :=
  VOASubalgebra.mem_generated_of_mem (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) (Ftrip_mem_tripGens p)

/-- The whole span of the generating set lies in `W(p)`. -/
theorem span_tripGens_le_tripletW (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    Submodule.span ℂ (tripGens p) ≤ (tripletW p hp).carrier :=
  Submodule.span_le.mpr (VOASubalgebra.subset_generated (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) (tripGens p))

/-- `e^{mα} ≠ 0`: a charged vacuum is a genuine state. -/
theorem latChargeGen_ne_zero (p : ℕ) (β : (latP p).carrier) :
    latChargeGen (latP p) β ≠ 0 :=
  Screen.latStateGen_ne_zero (latP p) (by rw [vacuumN]; exact one_ne_zero) β

/-- **`ω_λ ≠ 0`.**  If the conformal vector vanished then every Virasoro mode would vanish, so
`L₀` would act by `0`; but `L₀` acts by `1` on `e^α ∈ 𝒱₁`, and `e^α ≠ 0`. -/
theorem omegaTrip_ne_zero (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) : omegaTrip p ≠ 0 := by
  intro h
  refine latChargeGen_ne_zero p (alphaP p) ?_
  have hL := (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).L_zero_grading (latChargeGen (latP p) (alphaP p))
    (latChargeGen_alpha_mem_grade_one p hp)
  have hzero : (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).L 0 = 0 := by
    rw [VertexOperatorAlgebra.L_def, omegaTrip_eq_conformalVector p hp, h, map_zero]
    rfl
  rw [hzero] at hL
  simpa using hL.symm

/-- **`H ≠ 0`** (`Screen.Hscr_ne_zero`): `H` is the Schur state `S_{2p−1}(α) ⊗ e⁰` up to the
non-zero cocycle sign. -/
theorem Htrip_ne_zero (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) : Htrip p ≠ 0 :=
  Screen.Hscr_ne_zero (latP p) (latP_posDef p hp) (alphaP p) (alphaP_ne_zero p) p hp
    (latP_form_alpha p)

/-- **`F ≠ 0`** (`Screen.Fscr_ne_zero`). -/
theorem Ftrip_ne_zero (p : ℕ) : Ftrip p ≠ 0 :=
  Screen.Fscr_ne_zero (latP p) (alphaP p)

/-- **`W(p)` is non-trivial**: its carrier is not the zero submodule (it contains `H ≠ 0`). -/
theorem tripletW_carrier_ne_bot (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    (tripletW p hp).carrier ≠ ⊥ := by
  intro hbot
  exact Htrip_ne_zero p hp
    (Submodule.mem_bot ℂ |>.mp (hbot ▸ Htrip_mem_tripletW p hp))

/-- The generated VOA has a non-trivial carrier type: `W(p)` contains a non-zero vector. -/
theorem exists_ne_zero_tripletW (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    ∃ v : (tripletW p hp).carrier, v ≠ 0 :=
  ⟨⟨Htrip p, Htrip_mem_tripletW p hp⟩, fun h => Htrip_ne_zero p hp (congrArg Subtype.val h)⟩

/-! ## §6  The generating set is `piHom`-closed

`Core.VOASubalgebraGenerated.mem_generated` necessarily carries a clause for the homogeneous
projections `piHom`, because gradedness is an axiom of `VOASubalgebra`.  That clause is harmless
here: the generators are weight-homogeneous, so each `piHom n` either fixes a generator or kills
it, and the `piHom` closure of `tripGens p` is `tripGens p ∪ {0}`.  (The two levels `2` and
`2p − 1` never coincide, `2p − 1 = 2` having no solution in `ℤ`, but nothing below needs that.) -/

/-- `π_n` fixes a generator of weight `n`. -/
theorem piHom_omegaTrip_self (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    piHom (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) 2 (omegaTrip p) = omegaTrip p :=
  piHom_of_mem _ (omegaTrip_mem_grading p hp)

theorem piHom_Etrip_self (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    piHom (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) (2 * (p : ℤ) - 1) (Etrip p) = Etrip p :=
  piHom_of_mem _ (Etrip_mem_grading p hp)

theorem piHom_Htrip_self (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    piHom (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) (2 * (p : ℤ) - 1) (Htrip p) = Htrip p :=
  piHom_of_mem _ (Htrip_mem_grading p hp)

theorem piHom_Ftrip_self (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    piHom (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) (2 * (p : ℤ) - 1) (Ftrip p) = Ftrip p :=
  piHom_of_mem _ (Ftrip_mem_grading p hp)

/-- `π_n` kills a generator of a different weight. -/
theorem piHom_omegaTrip_zero (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) {n : ℤ} (hn : n ≠ 2) :
    piHom (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) n (omegaTrip p) = 0 :=
  piHom_of_mem_ne _ (Ne.symm hn) (omegaTrip_mem_grading p hp)

theorem piHom_Etrip_zero (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) {n : ℤ} (hn : n ≠ 2 * (p : ℤ) - 1) :
    piHom (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) n (Etrip p) = 0 :=
  piHom_of_mem_ne _ (Ne.symm hn) (Etrip_mem_grading p hp)

theorem piHom_Htrip_zero (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) {n : ℤ} (hn : n ≠ 2 * (p : ℤ) - 1) :
    piHom (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) n (Htrip p) = 0 :=
  piHom_of_mem_ne _ (Ne.symm hn) (Htrip_mem_grading p hp)

theorem piHom_Ftrip_zero (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) {n : ℤ} (hn : n ≠ 2 * (p : ℤ) - 1) :
    piHom (tripletLatticeVOA p hp) n (Ftrip p) = 0 :=
  piHom_of_mem_ne _ (Ne.symm hn) (Ftrip_mem_grading p hp)

/-- Every element of the generating set is homogeneous: each `x ∈ tripGens p` lies in a single
weight space (`2` for `ω_λ`, `2p − 1` for `E`, `H`, `F`).  Hence `π_n x ∈ {x, 0}` for every `n` and
the `piHom` clause of `mem_generated` never leaves the set. -/
theorem tripGens_homogeneous (p : ℕ) (hp : 1 ≤ p) :
    ∀ x ∈ tripGens p, ∃ k : ℤ, x ∈ (tripletLatticeVOA p hp).grading k := by
  intro x hx
  rcases hx with rfl | hx
  · exact ⟨2, omegaTrip_mem_grading p hp⟩
  rcases hx with rfl | hx
  · exact ⟨2 * (p : ℤ) - 1, Etrip_mem_grading p hp⟩
  rcases hx with rfl | hx
  · exact ⟨2 * (p : ℤ) - 1, Htrip_mem_grading p hp⟩
  · rw [Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hx
    subst hx
    exact ⟨2 * (p : ℤ) - 1, Ftrip_mem_grading p hp⟩

/-! ## §7  `p = 2`: a central-charge consistency check with `SympFerm.tripletW2`

At `p = 2` the Feigin–Fuchs value is `c = 1 − 6·1²/2 = −2`, the symplectic-fermion value.  The
existing `SympFerm.tripletW2` — built from symplectic fermions with **no** lattice, background
charge or screening operator — also has `c = −2`.

**This is a consistency check, nothing more.**  No isomorphism `W(2) ≅ SympFerm.tripletW2` is
proved or claimed here; the two VOAs live on different carrier types (`(tripletW 2 hp).carrier`
inside `V_{L_2}` versus `evenOdd QSF 0` inside the symplectic-fermion Fock space) and comparing them
is a research problem, deliberately not attempted. -/

/-- At `p = 2` the triplet algebra built here has central charge `−2`. -/
theorem tripletW_centralCharge_two (hp : 1 ≤ 2) :
    (tripletWVOA 2 hp).centralCharge = -2 := by
  rw [tripletW_centralCharge]
  norm_num

/-- **Consistency check (not an isomorphism):** `W(2)` assembled here from the deformed lattice VOA
and the symplectic-fermion `SympFerm.tripletW2` have the *same central charge*. -/
theorem tripletW_centralCharge_eq_tripletW2 (hp : 1 ≤ 2) :
    (tripletWVOA 2 hp).centralCharge = SympFerm.tripletW2.centralCharge := by
  rw [tripletW_centralCharge_two, SympFerm.tripletW2_centralCharge]

end VOA.LatGen.Wp
